Why a dual license
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The code is, and will remain, open source and free for the public under the
AGPL-3.0. The AGPL's copyleft and its network-use clause (section 13) require
that anyone who conveys the software — or offers it as a network service —
make their complete corresponding source available under the same terms.

Some organizations cannot or do not wish to comply with the AGPL's obligations
— for example, when embedding flowclock-cli in a proprietary product, shipping
it inside a closed-source distribution, or offering it as part of a hosted
service without releasing their own source. For those cases, a commercial
license removes the AGPL obligations in exchange for a commercial agreement.

